The koala's eyes are like two dark little pebbles sunken into a fluffy, grey ball of cotton. They stare out with a sleepy, half-lidded gaze, as if the koala is constantly fighting off the urge to take a nap right then and there. It's like the koala is perpetually confused, trying to figure out which tree branch it should nap on next. Those beady little eyes may look cute and cuddly, but they also give the impression that the koala is silently judging your every move, just waiting for you to provide a nice, comfortable eucalyptus leaf for it to munch on.\
