Lieutenant Shakti was the public face of the Department of Traffic Movement and Property Security, formerly known as the Police. He appeared in all of the recruiting advertisements, made public affairs announcements and was now making a name for himself as a homicide investigator. The fact that he had been called to a run-of-the-mill suicide seemed odd, but if it was something more sinister, the entire floor would still be crawling with cops, robots, flashing lights and all manner of devices that beeped. \cf2 \
\
